## Clipping Distinctions

Top/bottom neighboring-question fragments are vertical/off-window incompleteness, not horizontal right-tail failures. In `0017`, the upper B fraction is cut vertically at the image top. In `0065` C/D and `0073` Q8 B, leading expression content is incomplete; the visible right-hand suffixes are not missing. In `0077`/`0080`, the diagram loses left-side content, while `h` and the observed text tails remain visible. No missing text, region, endpoint, or option is invented.

Exact visible Chinese right-tail text is recorded as JSON Unicode escapes in `result.json`; it decodes to the observed glyphs. Slashes separating text lines indicate visible wrapping, not characters in the screenshots. All image paths, hashes, region-specific PASS/BLOCKED decisions, and terminal details are recorded there.

The assignment's two figure-region metadata objects are preserved verbatim in the result. Their coordinate system is not established by this observation; they are not treated as screenshot crops or proof of unseen pixels.

